diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 65cd5e3..6f3de84 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -37,6 +37,9 @@ Modes are available depending on your system type:
 - Hybrid(kept as a default mode, everything goes back to unblocked)
 - Manual
 
+**Laptops with a live display mux** (patched nvidia-modeset exposing the `mux` parameter, e.g. ASUS ROG Zephyrus G14 2025)
+- Ultimate (Hybrid, plus the internal panel driven directly by the dGPU, switched live)
+
 ## How it works
 
 Cardwire uses eBPF with LSM hooks to intercept file operations on GPU device nodes, such as `/dev/dri/renderDX`, `/dev/dri/cardX`, sysfs `config`, `nvidiaX` and other GPU-related files.
